{"jobs":[{"id":"f53d1e36-48aa-4dd9-845b-032b62172244","title":"Staff Software Engineer (Fullstack)","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"USA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Brooklyn, NYC","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Brooklyn"}}}],"publishedAt":"2024-08-16T21:04:23.259+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/f53d1e36-48aa-4dd9-845b-032b62172244","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/f53d1e36-48aa-4dd9-845b-032b62172244/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is on a mission to build technology that strengthens the social safety net. We’re a passionate team of ~100 Propellers who envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Are you a Fullstack Engineer looking to make a big impact at a mission-driven company? Do you thrive in high-autonomy startup environments? </strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a motivated <strong>Fullstack Engineer</strong> to join our engineering team at Propel to help make this a reality. This role includes opportunities to flex between IC and engineering management and team leadership!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This role will make an impact and possibly work across several products and stacks, including interacting with government programs, surfacing savings opportunities, enrolling users in healthcare plans, internal tooling, architecture, and more!</strong> We are looking for a passionate, user-centric fullstack engineer that is excited about working on meaningful and complex technical problems that have a positive impact on our users’ lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Here's how you'll impact the company:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Be a strategic leader in identifying the best technical and product opportunities. </strong>Whether it’s hopping in to build a service from scratch to support a new product line or advocating for a large refactor of a legacy system, this role will have a strong voice in setting the technical and product direction of the company and be hands-on in making it happen. You will likely be asked to lead a team at various points and be flexible in going between impactful IC work and leadership responsibilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Up-level and set the bar for engineering. </strong>You will be a role model for others and establish best practices when it comes to technical decisions, code hygiene, written communication and documentation, and judgment when it comes to shipping high-quality products and projects on a timeline.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Dive deep into the most important, highest complexity problems at the company. </strong>When there is something that needs to get done at high complexity and scale, you’ll be someone we lean on to help get it done. You’ll be given both a lot of autonomy and a lot of support in how you want to tackle tough but rewarding challenges!</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">10+ years experience in designing, building, shipping, and maintaining complex full-stack software at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years experience successfully leading and managing a team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in at least one backend and one frontend language, with a willingness to learn Python and JavaScript</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working in a startup environment and possess the ability to operate effectively and independently when faced with ambiguity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to ramp up quickly to our product ecosystem to contribute to large and impactful projects</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills across technical and non-technical audiences and topics, both written and verbal</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to provide excellent feedback in technical specs, code reviews, and team discussions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for making a difference in the lives of our users</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional candidates will have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of identifying the right problems to solve, advocating for and driving change, and keeping stakeholders in the loop</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with building consumer-facing product(s) for large user bases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexibility in operating as a pure individual contributor or as a manager of a small team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity and excitement when confronted with new technologies, stacks, or novel problems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent judgment when trading off speed of shipping vs. robustness and scalability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ability to adapt and communicate smoothly across all levels of seniority</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A focus on impact and ability to prioritize both long-term and short term needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Eagerness to participate at the strategic level when it comes to the technical and product roadmap and prioritization on the organization-level</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion and skill for mentoring and up-leveling other engineers</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Propel, you'll enjoy:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meaningful work and a strong, shared sense of mission with a passionate and world-class team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote-friendly work environment with a dog-friendly office in Downtown Brooklyn</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">20 days of PTO and unlimited sick days</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% 401K match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Other health and mental health focused benefits and perks </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel builds compensation bands referencing the 75th percentile of compensation for companies like us. <em>Expected</em> compensation for the role as scoped is <strong>$240K - $270K</strong> and will be based on how a candidate matches to our internal leveling guide. Bands may be expanded if someone is leveled more senior than the role was initially scoped.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Considerations:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes <strong>California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington.</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Background Check Requirement: </strong>For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>More About Propel</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like Vote.org, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Learn more about our impact from the press</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong>Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&amp;utm_medium=member_desktop&amp;rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\"><strong>Late Show With Stephen Colbert</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\"><strong>How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&amp;smid=sl-share\"><strong>How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\"><strong>How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong>Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\"><strong>How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond</strong></a></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Join us, and let's build something amazing together!</strong></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us\n\nPropel is on a mission to build technology that strengthens the social safety net. We’re a passionate team of ~100 Propellers who envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.\n\nThe Role\n\nAre you a Fullstack Engineer looking to make a big impact at a mission-driven company? Do you thrive in high-autonomy startup environments? \n\nWe’re looking for a motivated Fullstack Engineer to join our engineering team at Propel to help make this a reality. This role includes opportunities to flex between IC and engineering management and team leadership!\n\nThis role will make an impact and possibly work across several products and stacks, including interacting with government programs, surfacing savings opportunities, enrolling users in healthcare plans, internal tooling, architecture, and more! We are looking for a passionate, user-centric fullstack engineer that is excited about working on meaningful and complex technical problems that have a positive impact on our users’ lives.\n\nHere's how you'll impact the company:\n\n - Be a strategic leader in identifying the best technical and product opportunities. Whether it’s hopping in to build a service from scratch to support a new product line or advocating for a large refactor of a legacy system, this role will have a strong voice in setting the technical and product direction of the company and be hands-on in making it happen. You will likely be asked to lead a team at various points and be flexible in going between impactful IC work and leadership responsibilities.\n\n - Up-level and set the bar for engineering. You will be a role model for others and establish best practices when it comes to technical decisions, code hygiene, written communication and documentation, and judgment when it comes to shipping high-quality products and projects on a timeline.\n\n - Dive deep into the most important, highest complexity problems at the company. When there is something that needs to get done at high complexity and scale, you’ll be someone we lean on to help get it done. You’ll be given both a lot of autonomy and a lot of support in how you want to tackle tough but rewarding challenges!\n\nRequirements:\n\n - 10+ years experience in designing, building, shipping, and maintaining complex full-stack software at scale\n\n - 3+ years experience successfully leading and managing a team\n\n - Fluency in at least one backend and one frontend language, with a willingness to learn Python and JavaScript\n\n - Experience working in a startup environment and possess the ability to operate effectively and independently when faced with ambiguity\n\n - Ability to ramp up quickly to our product ecosystem to contribute to large and impactful projects\n\n - Excellent communication skills across technical and non-technical audiences and topics, both written and verbal\n\n - Ability to provide excellent feedback in technical specs, code reviews, and team discussions\n\n - Passion for making a difference in the lives of our users\n\nExceptional candidates will have:\n\n - A track record of identifying the right problems to solve, advocating for and driving change, and keeping stakeholders in the loop\n\n - Experience with building consumer-facing product(s) for large user bases\n\n - Flexibility in operating as a pure individual contributor or as a manager of a small team\n\n - Curiosity and excitement when confronted with new technologies, stacks, or novel problems\n\n - Excellent judgment when trading off speed of shipping vs. robustness and scalability\n\n - The ability to adapt and communicate smoothly across all levels of seniority\n\n - A focus on impact and ability to prioritize both long-term and short term needs\n\n - Eagerness to participate at the strategic level when it comes to the technical and product roadmap and prioritization on the organization-level\n\n - Passion and skill for mentoring and up-leveling other engineers\n\nAt Propel, you'll enjoy:\n\n - Meaningful work and a strong, shared sense of mission with a passionate and world-class team\n\n - Remote-friendly work environment with a dog-friendly office in Downtown Brooklyn\n\n - 20 days of PTO and unlimited sick days\n\n - 4% 401K match\n\n - $10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility\n\n - Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options\n\n - Other health and mental health focused benefits and perks \n\n - Propel builds compensation bands referencing the 75th percentile of compensation for companies like us. Expected compensation for the role as scoped is $240K - $270K and will be based on how a candidate matches to our internal leveling guide. Bands may be expanded if someone is leveled more senior than the role was initially scoped.\n\nAdditional Considerations:\n\n - We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.\n\n - We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington.\n\n - Background Check Requirement: For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).\n\nMore About Propel\n\nPropel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like Vote.org, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly.\n\nPropel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.\n\nLearn more about our impact from the press\n\n - Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - Late Show With Stephen Colbert http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\n\n - How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\n\n - How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share\n\n - How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\n\n - Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\n\nJoin us, and let's build something amazing together!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e6a61c7b-87bb-448c-81c7-2db5a2bb1d9f","title":"Senior Full Stack Engineer, Healthcare","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"USA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Brooklyn, NYC","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Brooklyn"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-28T15:16:53.531+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/e6a61c7b-87bb-448c-81c7-2db5a2bb1d9f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/e6a61c7b-87bb-448c-81c7-2db5a2bb1d9f/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel builds technology that strengthens the social safety net in America. We envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The safety net’s strength depends not just on funding, but delivery. Propel exists to dramatically improve how government benefits are delivered. Managing SNAP benefits, picking a D-SNP plan, or protecting against EBT theft should feel as seamless as Apple Pay or Netflix.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Governments struggle to build modern, scalable user experiences. We don’t.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Over 5.5 million Americans trust Propel today. We’ve grown revenue 35% YoY and are reinventing entire benefit categories, including Medicare, around the real needs of low-income Americans. We’re building a high-growth, high-ceiling, sustainable for-profit company where impact drives revenue.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Are you a Senior Fullstack Engineer looking to build 0→1 products at a mission-driven company? Do you enjoy creating consumer-grade experiences and thrive in high-autonomy startup environments?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a motivated Senior Fullstack Engineer to join Propel and help build new Medicare and Medicaid products from the ground up. In this role, you’ll work end-to-end across frontend and backend systems to develop user experiences that help people understand coverage options, surface savings opportunities, and enroll in healthcare plans. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll collaborate closely with product and design, and help shape technical architecture, internal tooling, and scalable integrations with healthcare and government systems.</p><h2></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What we offer:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An engineering culture that is humble, motivated, and collaborative </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistent knowledge sharing through projects or bugs demos, Lunch &amp; Learn presentations, and documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A people-first approach to management where we value engineers’ voices, support career development, and offer opportunities for technical growth that interest you</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A remote-first working environment. Our headquarters is in Brooklyn and we have a co-working monthly stipend for employees outside of NYC. We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes<strong> California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland</strong>, <strong>Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington.</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">20 Days of PTO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% 401K match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fair, equitable, and competitive salaries. Propel believes that everyone should be compensated fairly and equitably. We set our salary ranges using compensation data from hundreds of NYC based startups at our stage. Additionally, pay is not determined based on location. The salary range for this position is <strong>$170,000 - $230,000</strong> depending on experience and interview performance. Equity and excellent benefits come with this position as well!</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you will do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build software systems used by millions of low-income Americans, helping to put dollars back in their pockets</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build iOS and Android apps using Vue + TypeScript + Capacitor</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop significant server-side software using Python and Flask, backed by Postgres and Redis; leverage AWS offerings as well as other open source technologies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Create software that is reliable, scalable, and maintainable</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Effectively communicate with team members during projects, code review, etc.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to building our engineering culture and processes as we continue to scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate on deciding on the right projects, building great solutions, and helping your team succeed</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with our Product and Design team to scope projects and execute on innovative products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in our on-call rotation</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience designing, building, shipping, and maintaining complex full-stack software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with a startup environment or the ability to operate effectively when faced with ambiguity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excitement to dive deep into our codebase and product ecosystem to contribute to large and impactful projects</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication skills across technical and non-technical audiences and topics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Eagerness to learn and actively contribute to team discussions, design doc reviews, and code reviews</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Computer science degree or equivalent fundamentals learned elsewhere</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in Python and JavaScript or a willingness to learn and specialize in these languages</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for making a difference in the lives of our users</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice to have: Experience with or knowledge of government services, particularly safety net services like SNAP, WIC, TANF, SSI, SSDI, Medicaid, Section 8</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Considerations:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes <strong>California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Background Check Requirement:</strong> For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>More About Propel</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like Vote.org, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors, including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Learn more about our impact from the press</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong>Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&amp;utm_medium=member_desktop&amp;rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\"><strong>Late Show With Stephen Colbert</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\"><strong>How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&amp;smid=sl-share\"><strong>How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\"><strong>How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong>Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\"><strong>How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond</strong></a></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Join us, and let's build something amazing together!</strong></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us\n\nPropel builds technology that strengthens the social safety net in America. We envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.\n\nThe safety net’s strength depends not just on funding, but delivery. Propel exists to dramatically improve how government benefits are delivered. Managing SNAP benefits, picking a D-SNP plan, or protecting against EBT theft should feel as seamless as Apple Pay or Netflix.\n\nGovernments struggle to build modern, scalable user experiences. We don’t.\n\nOver 5.5 million Americans trust Propel today. We’ve grown revenue 35% YoY and are reinventing entire benefit categories, including Medicare, around the real needs of low-income Americans. We’re building a high-growth, high-ceiling, sustainable for-profit company where impact drives revenue.\n\nThe Role\n\nAre you a Senior Fullstack Engineer looking to build 0→1 products at a mission-driven company? Do you enjoy creating consumer-grade experiences and thrive in high-autonomy startup environments?\n\nWe’re looking for a motivated Senior Fullstack Engineer to join Propel and help build new Medicare and Medicaid products from the ground up. In this role, you’ll work end-to-end across frontend and backend systems to develop user experiences that help people understand coverage options, surface savings opportunities, and enroll in healthcare plans. \n\nYou’ll collaborate closely with product and design, and help shape technical architecture, internal tooling, and scalable integrations with healthcare and government systems.\n\n\n\n\nWhat we offer:\n\n - An engineering culture that is humble, motivated, and collaborative \n\n - Consistent knowledge sharing through projects or bugs demos, Lunch & Learn presentations, and documentation\n\n - A people-first approach to management where we value engineers’ voices, support career development, and offer opportunities for technical growth that interest you\n\n - Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission\n\n - A remote-first working environment. Our headquarters is in Brooklyn and we have a co-working monthly stipend for employees outside of NYC. We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington.\n\n - 20 Days of PTO\n\n - 4% 401K match\n\n - $10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility\n\n - Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options\n\n - Fair, equitable, and competitive salaries. Propel believes that everyone should be compensated fairly and equitably. We set our salary ranges using compensation data from hundreds of NYC based startups at our stage. Additionally, pay is not determined based on location. The salary range for this position is $170,000 - $230,000 depending on experience and interview performance. Equity and excellent benefits come with this position as well!\n\nWhat you will do:\n\n - Build software systems used by millions of low-income Americans, helping to put dollars back in their pockets\n\n - Build iOS and Android apps using Vue + TypeScript + Capacitor\n\n - Develop significant server-side software using Python and Flask, backed by Postgres and Redis; leverage AWS offerings as well as other open source technologies\n\n - Create software that is reliable, scalable, and maintainable\n\n - Effectively communicate with team members during projects, code review, etc.\n\n - Contribute to building our engineering culture and processes as we continue to scale\n\n - Collaborate on deciding on the right projects, building great solutions, and helping your team succeed\n\n - Work with our Product and Design team to scope projects and execute on innovative products\n\n - Participate in our on-call rotation\n\nWhat you have:\n\n - 5+ years of experience designing, building, shipping, and maintaining complex full-stack software\n\n - Experience with a startup environment or the ability to operate effectively when faced with ambiguity\n\n - Excitement to dive deep into our codebase and product ecosystem to contribute to large and impactful projects\n\n - Strong communication skills across technical and non-technical audiences and topics\n\n - Eagerness to learn and actively contribute to team discussions, design doc reviews, and code reviews\n\n - Computer science degree or equivalent fundamentals learned elsewhere\n\n - Fluency in Python and JavaScript or a willingness to learn and specialize in these languages\n\n - Passion for making a difference in the lives of our users\n\n - Nice to have: Experience with or knowledge of government services, particularly safety net services like SNAP, WIC, TANF, SSI, SSDI, Medicaid, Section 8\n\nAdditional Considerations:\n\n - We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.\n\n - We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington.\n\n - Background Check Requirement: For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).\n\nMore About Propel\n\nPropel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like Vote.org, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly. \n\nPropel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors, including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.\n\nLearn more about our impact from the press\n\n - Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - Late Show With Stephen Colbert http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\n\n - How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\n\n - How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share\n\n - How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\n\n - Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\n\nJoin us, and let's build something amazing together!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"11265618-fbca-405c-b52f-a9b85ffe6aed","title":"Senior Platform Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"USA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Brooklyn, NYC","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Brooklyn"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-04-01T12:19:20.490+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/11265618-fbca-405c-b52f-a9b85ffe6aed","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/11265618-fbca-405c-b52f-a9b85ffe6aed/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is on a mission to build technology that strengthens the social safety net. We’re a passionate team of ~100 Propellers who envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Are you a Platform Engineer looking to make a big impact on a mission-driven company? Do you enjoy architecting software that shapes an entire engineering organization? Do you thrive in high-autonomy startup environments?</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a self-motivated <strong>Senior Platform Engineer</strong> to join our Developer Enablement Team within the engineering org at Propel.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This role empowers other engineers by improving the cloud native platforms that enable development and delivery of Propel’s technology.</strong> These cloud native platforms impact several products and stacks, including interacting with government programs, surfacing savings opportunities, enrolling users in healthcare plans, internal tooling, architecture, and more! Your focus will be on running fault tolerant applications in Kubernetes and AWS, and solving organization-wide engineering problems. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for a tinkerer to experiment with improvements to the developer experience at Propel. You will architect new features for our cloud platform, support a wide-variety of production applications, address technical debt, and help guide other engineers.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What we offer:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An engineering culture that is humble, motivated, and collaborative </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistent knowledge sharing through projects or bugs demos, Lunch &amp; Learn presentations, and documentation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A people-first approach to management where we value engineers’ voices, support career development, and offer opportunities for technical growth that interest you</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A remote-first working environment. Our headquarters is in Brooklyn and we have a co-working monthly stipend for employees outside of NYC. We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes<strong> California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland</strong>, <strong>Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington.</strong></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fair, equitable, and competitive salaries. Propel believes that everyone should be compensated fairly and equitably. We set our salary ranges using compensation data from hundreds of NYC based startups at our stage. Additionally, pay is not determined based on location. The salary range for this position is <strong>$170,000 - $240,000</strong> depending on experience and interview performance. Equity and excellent benefits come with this position as well!</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">20 Days of PTO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% 401K match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you will do:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own our fundamental cloud services and tooling.</strong> You will manage our cloud networks, security policies, and other low-level cloud services. Our engineering team provisions cloud infrastructure on top of this foundation, using infrastructure as code tools like Terraform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own our application platform. </strong>You will administer our Kubernetes clusters to meet the needs of the engineering team. You will explore new tools and services that improve the security and reliability of our applications running on the platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own our developer experience. </strong>You will assist engineers with best practices for using and deploying to the platform. You will administer our CI/CD and other internal tools to make this as easy as possible.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What you have:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years experience in DevOps, Site Reliability Engineering, Platform Engineering, or Systems Engineering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Proficient with at least one high-level programming language - Python, Go, or whatever else you like</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of networking, containers, security and scalability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong Kubernetes fundamentals and experience with Helm or other common tools in the ecosystem</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong infrastructure as code skills (we use Terraform)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Broad experience across many cloud services within a major cloud provider (we use AWS)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with observability platforms (we use Datadog)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience writing CI/CD pipelines (we use GitHub Actions)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience being part of an on-call rotation to fix urgent issues</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The following are nice to have but not required:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Kubernetes tools such as Vault, Sealed Secrets, Consul, Prometheus, etc.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with data platforms such as Snowflake, and experience building and managing data infrastructure</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Cybersecurity and/or regulatory compliance experience (HIPAA, SOC 2, ISO 27001, etc)</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Considerations:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>More About Propel</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like Vote.org, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors, including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Learn more about our impact from the press</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong>Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&amp;utm_medium=member_desktop&amp;rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\"><strong>Late Show With Stephen Colbert</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\"><strong>How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&amp;smid=sl-share\"><strong>How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\"><strong>How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong>Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\"><strong>How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond</strong></a></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Join us, and let's build something amazing together!</strong></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us\n\nPropel is on a mission to build technology that strengthens the social safety net. We’re a passionate team of ~100 Propellers who envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.\n\nThe Role\n\nAre you a Platform Engineer looking to make a big impact on a mission-driven company? Do you enjoy architecting software that shapes an entire engineering organization? Do you thrive in high-autonomy startup environments?\n\nWe’re looking for a self-motivated Senior Platform Engineer to join our Developer Enablement Team within the engineering org at Propel.\n\nThis role empowers other engineers by improving the cloud native platforms that enable development and delivery of Propel’s technology. These cloud native platforms impact several products and stacks, including interacting with government programs, surfacing savings opportunities, enrolling users in healthcare plans, internal tooling, architecture, and more! Your focus will be on running fault tolerant applications in Kubernetes and AWS, and solving organization-wide engineering problems. \n\nWe are looking for a tinkerer to experiment with improvements to the developer experience at Propel. You will architect new features for our cloud platform, support a wide-variety of production applications, address technical debt, and help guide other engineers.\n\nWhat we offer:\n\n - An engineering culture that is humble, motivated, and collaborative \n\n - Consistent knowledge sharing through projects or bugs demos, Lunch & Learn presentations, and documentation\n\n - A people-first approach to management where we value engineers’ voices, support career development, and offer opportunities for technical growth that interest you\n\n - Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission\n\n - A remote-first working environment. Our headquarters is in Brooklyn and we have a co-working monthly stipend for employees outside of NYC. We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington.\n\n - Fair, equitable, and competitive salaries. Propel believes that everyone should be compensated fairly and equitably. We set our salary ranges using compensation data from hundreds of NYC based startups at our stage. Additionally, pay is not determined based on location. The salary range for this position is $170,000 - $240,000 depending on experience and interview performance. Equity and excellent benefits come with this position as well!\n\n - 20 Days of PTO\n\n - 4% 401K match\n\n - $10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility\n\n - Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options\n\nWhat you will do:\n\n - Own our fundamental cloud services and tooling. You will manage our cloud networks, security policies, and other low-level cloud services. Our engineering team provisions cloud infrastructure on top of this foundation, using infrastructure as code tools like Terraform.\n\n - Own our application platform. You will administer our Kubernetes clusters to meet the needs of the engineering team. You will explore new tools and services that improve the security and reliability of our applications running on the platform.\n\n - Own our developer experience. You will assist engineers with best practices for using and deploying to the platform. You will administer our CI/CD and other internal tools to make this as easy as possible.\n\nWhat you have:\n\n - 5+ years experience in DevOps, Site Reliability Engineering, Platform Engineering, or Systems Engineering\n\n - Proficient with at least one high-level programming language - Python, Go, or whatever else you like\n\n - Strong understanding of networking, containers, security and scalability\n\n - Strong Kubernetes fundamentals and experience with Helm or other common tools in the ecosystem\n\n - Strong infrastructure as code skills (we use Terraform)\n\n - Broad experience across many cloud services within a major cloud provider (we use AWS)\n\n - Experience with observability platforms (we use Datadog)\n\n - Experience writing CI/CD pipelines (we use GitHub Actions)\n\n - Experience being part of an on-call rotation to fix urgent issues\n\n - The following are nice to have but not required:\n   \n   - Experience with Kubernetes tools such as Vault, Sealed Secrets, Consul, Prometheus, etc.\n   \n   - Experience with data platforms such as Snowflake, and experience building and managing data infrastructure\n   \n   - Cybersecurity and/or regulatory compliance experience (HIPAA, SOC 2, ISO 27001, etc)\n\nAdditional Considerations:\n\n - We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.\n\nMore About Propel\n\nPropel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like Vote.org, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly. \n\nPropel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors, including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.\n\nLearn more about our impact from the press\n\n - Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - Late Show With Stephen Colbert http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\n\n - How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\n\n - How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share\n\n - How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\n\n - Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\n\nJoin us, and let's build something amazing together!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"f910f4b4-e42d-4bb8-b5b2-c464ba7ff6b4","title":"Medicare Advisor","department":"New Ventures","team":"Healthcare","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"USA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Brooklyn, NYC","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Brooklyn"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-07-30T00:54:36.326+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/f910f4b4-e42d-4bb8-b5b2-c464ba7ff6b4","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/f910f4b4-e42d-4bb8-b5b2-c464ba7ff6b4/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Us</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel builds technology that strengthens the social safety net in America. We envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The safety net’s strength depends not just on funding, but delivery. Propel exists to dramatically improve how government benefits are delivered. Managing SNAP benefits, picking a D-SNP plan, or protecting against EBT theft should feel as seamless as Apple Pay or Netflix.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Governments struggle to build modern, scalable user experiences. We don’t.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Over 5.5 million Americans trust Propel today. We’ve grown revenue 35% YoY and are reinventing entire benefit categories, including Medicare, around the real needs of low-income Americans. We’re building a high-growth, high-ceiling, sustainable for-profit company where impact drives revenue.</p><h2></h2><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel serves approximately 1M users who are Medicare eligible, most of whom are also Medicaid eligible. We are building the first-ever app-based brokerage focused on helping \"duals\" (Americans on Medicare and Medicaid) enroll in healthcare plans. We specialize in Dual Eligible Special Needs Plans (D-SNPs) and are expanding to 30 states in 2026, with plans to move into larger Medicare markets over the next 24 months. As a Medicare Advisor, you will be a trusted expert, helping users compare Medicare plans, enroll with confidence, and maximize their healthcare benefits. You will also collaborate with our EPD (engineering, product, design) team to refine how we support users in navigating government healthcare.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role requires someone who is comfortable using AI tools in their daily work to research plans, draft communications, summarize complex information, and improve personal productivity. You should be an enthusiastic and capable user of modern AI-powered tools.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to incoming inquiries from users regarding D-SNPs, Traditional Medicare, Medicare Advantage plans, and Medicaid, providing expert guidance and support via in-app chat (primary) and phone (secondary).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Use AI-powered tools to efficiently research plan details, compare coverage options, and synthesize complex regulatory information for users.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Apply a user-centric approach, prioritizing user needs and exceeding service expectations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conduct comprehensive comparisons of Medicare Advantage plans, ensuring users understand their options for healthcare coverage based on their specific needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Educate users on eligibility requirements, enrollment processes, and Medicare compliance, helping them navigate the complexities of healthcare regulations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Execute enrollment applications accurately, providing users with critical information about deadlines and ongoing actions needed to sustain their coverage effectively.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain appointments with multiple insurance carriers across 30+ states and ensure compliance with licensing requirements as Propel expands its D-SNP footprint.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with product, design, and engineering teams to improve app functionality, offering insights from user interactions and enrollment experiences.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage AI tools to draft user communications, create summaries, and identify patterns in user inquiries that can inform product improvements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Offer constructive feedback to enhance user and agent experiences within the application workflow.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flex outside of core D-SNP advisory as needed, supporting broader Medicare enrollment efforts, general app CX, and other team initiatives as we scale into new states and markets.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>This Role Might Not Be the Right Fit If</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe in being upfront so you can make the best decision for yourself. Propel is a startup, and our healthcare team is still building many of the processes and playbooks that larger organizations already have in place. That is exciting, but it is not for everyone, and that is completely okay.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role may not be the right fit if:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You prefer a structured environment with established workflows and detailed guidance for every situation. We are still writing the playbook here.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You do best with consistent, close oversight before taking action. Our team operates with a high degree of autonomy and trust.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are looking for a role where the scope of your work is unlikely to change. We are growing fast, expanding into new states, and adapting constantly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are not comfortable using technology or AI tools as part of your daily workflow. We are a tech company at our core, and our advisors work alongside AI every day.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">There is nothing wrong with any of these preferences. We share this because we want you to succeed, and setting clear expectations is part of how we do that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Required Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fast learner with a strong interest in developing expertise in Medicare/Medicaid nationwide.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable using AI tools (such as ChatGPT, Claude, or similar) in daily work for tasks like research, drafting, and problem-solving. Willingness to learn and adopt new AI-powered tools as they are introduced.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to handle complex user inquiries and multitask while receiving information from a user, including researching health plans and concepts.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Quickly develops credibility with users, demonstrating an aptitude for active listening, deep knowledge in the area you are advising them on, and providing confident consultations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Have or are willing to obtain an active broker/agent health insurance license in your home state and additional non-resident state licensure (company-sponsored).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willing to complete training and take tests relevant to getting appointed by health insurance carriers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent communication skills with the ability to explain complex concepts simply.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A comprehensive understanding of the difficulties faced by low-income Americans and a dedication to offering compassionate and tailored assistance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">From October 15th through December 7th (the Annual Enrollment Period), refrain from taking vacation and be able to take phone/chat shifts on the weekends (likely 1 day/weekend during that period).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Must pass a background check as part of the hiring process.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Bonus</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in Spanish.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior experience in healthcare, insurance, benefits counseling, or customer service roles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working at a startup or tech company.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>At Propel, you'll enjoy</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote-friendly work environment with a dog-friendly office in Downtown Brooklyn. The team meets in-person for optional retreats.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">20 Days of PTO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% 401K match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Other health and mental health focused benefits and perks </p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel believes that everyone should be compensated fairly and equitably. We set our salary ranges using compensation data from hundreds of NYC-based startups at our stage. Additionally, pay is not determined based on location. Compensation for this position includes base salary and a performance-based bonus. The expected base salary for the role is <strong>$70,000 - $80,000</strong>. </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Considerations:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interview Accommodations:</strong> Propel is committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the interview process. If you need accommodations due to a disability or medical condition (such as additional time or accessibility support), please let us know as early as possible so we can support you appropriately.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes <strong>California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Background Check Requirement:</strong> For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>More About Propel</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like Vote.org, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Learn more about our impact from the press</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong>Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp</strong></a></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&amp;utm_medium=member_desktop&amp;rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\"><strong>Late Show With Stephen Colbert</strong></a></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\"><strong>How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America</strong></a></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&amp;smid=sl-share\"><strong>How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid</strong></a></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\"><strong>How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients</strong></a></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong>Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown</strong></a></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\"><strong>How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond</strong></a></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Join us, and let's build something amazing together!</strong></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT US\n\nPropel builds technology that strengthens the social safety net in America. We envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.\n\nThe safety net’s strength depends not just on funding, but delivery. Propel exists to dramatically improve how government benefits are delivered. Managing SNAP benefits, picking a D-SNP plan, or protecting against EBT theft should feel as seamless as Apple Pay or Netflix.\n\nGovernments struggle to build modern, scalable user experiences. We don’t.\n\nOver 5.5 million Americans trust Propel today. We’ve grown revenue 35% YoY and are reinventing entire benefit categories, including Medicare, around the real needs of low-income Americans. We’re building a high-growth, high-ceiling, sustainable for-profit company where impact drives revenue.\n\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nPropel serves approximately 1M users who are Medicare eligible, most of whom are also Medicaid eligible. We are building the first-ever app-based brokerage focused on helping \"duals\" (Americans on Medicare and Medicaid) enroll in healthcare plans. We specialize in Dual Eligible Special Needs Plans (D-SNPs) and are expanding to 30 states in 2026, with plans to move into larger Medicare markets over the next 24 months. As a Medicare Advisor, you will be a trusted expert, helping users compare Medicare plans, enroll with confidence, and maximize their healthcare benefits. You will also collaborate with our EPD (engineering, product, design) team to refine how we support users in navigating government healthcare.\n\nThis role requires someone who is comfortable using AI tools in their daily work to research plans, draft communications, summarize complex information, and improve personal productivity. You should be an enthusiastic and capable user of modern AI-powered tools.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Respond to incoming inquiries from users regarding D-SNPs, Traditional Medicare, Medicare Advantage plans, and Medicaid, providing expert guidance and support via in-app chat (primary) and phone (secondary).\n\n - Use AI-powered tools to efficiently research plan details, compare coverage options, and synthesize complex regulatory information for users.\n\n - Apply a user-centric approach, prioritizing user needs and exceeding service expectations.\n\n - Conduct comprehensive comparisons of Medicare Advantage plans, ensuring users understand their options for healthcare coverage based on their specific needs.\n\n - Educate users on eligibility requirements, enrollment processes, and Medicare compliance, helping them navigate the complexities of healthcare regulations.\n\n - Execute enrollment applications accurately, providing users with critical information about deadlines and ongoing actions needed to sustain their coverage effectively.\n\n - Maintain appointments with multiple insurance carriers across 30+ states and ensure compliance with licensing requirements as Propel expands its D-SNP footprint.\n\n - Collaborate with product, design, and engineering teams to improve app functionality, offering insights from user interactions and enrollment experiences.\n\n - Leverage AI tools to draft user communications, create summaries, and identify patterns in user inquiries that can inform product improvements.\n\n - Offer constructive feedback to enhance user and agent experiences within the application workflow.\n\n - Flex outside of core D-SNP advisory as needed, supporting broader Medicare enrollment efforts, general app CX, and other team initiatives as we scale into new states and markets.\n\n\nTHIS ROLE MIGHT NOT BE THE RIGHT FIT IF\n\nWe believe in being upfront so you can make the best decision for yourself. Propel is a startup, and our healthcare team is still building many of the processes and playbooks that larger organizations already have in place. That is exciting, but it is not for everyone, and that is completely okay.\n\nThis role may not be the right fit if:\n\n - You prefer a structured environment with established workflows and detailed guidance for every situation. We are still writing the playbook here.\n\n - You do best with consistent, close oversight before taking action. Our team operates with a high degree of autonomy and trust.\n\n - You are looking for a role where the scope of your work is unlikely to change. We are growing fast, expanding into new states, and adapting constantly.\n\n - You are not comfortable using technology or AI tools as part of your daily workflow. We are a tech company at our core, and our advisors work alongside AI every day.\n\nThere is nothing wrong with any of these preferences. We share this because we want you to succeed, and setting clear expectations is part of how we do that.\n\n\n\n\nREQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Fast learner with a strong interest in developing expertise in Medicare/Medicaid nationwide.\n\n - Comfortable using AI tools (such as ChatGPT, Claude, or similar) in daily work for tasks like research, drafting, and problem-solving. Willingness to learn and adopt new AI-powered tools as they are introduced.\n\n - Able to handle complex user inquiries and multitask while receiving information from a user, including researching health plans and concepts.\n\n - Quickly develops credibility with users, demonstrating an aptitude for active listening, deep knowledge in the area you are advising them on, and providing confident consultations.\n\n - Have or are willing to obtain an active broker/agent health insurance license in your home state and additional non-resident state licensure (company-sponsored).\n\n - Willing to complete training and take tests relevant to getting appointed by health insurance carriers.\n\n - Excellent communication skills with the ability to explain complex concepts simply.\n\n - A comprehensive understanding of the difficulties faced by low-income Americans and a dedication to offering compassionate and tailored assistance.\n\n - From October 15th through December 7th (the Annual Enrollment Period), refrain from taking vacation and be able to take phone/chat shifts on the weekends (likely 1 day/weekend during that period).\n\n - Must pass a background check as part of the hiring process.\n\n\nBONUS\n\n - Fluency in Spanish.\n\n - Prior experience in healthcare, insurance, benefits counseling, or customer service roles.\n\n - Experience working at a startup or tech company.\n\n\nAT PROPEL, YOU'LL ENJOY\n\n - Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission\n\n - Remote-friendly work environment with a dog-friendly office in Downtown Brooklyn. The team meets in-person for optional retreats.\n\n - 20 Days of PTO\n\n - 4% 401K match\n\n - $10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility\n\n - Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options\n\n - Other health and mental health focused benefits and perks \n\n - Propel believes that everyone should be compensated fairly and equitably. We set our salary ranges using compensation data from hundreds of NYC-based startups at our stage. Additionally, pay is not determined based on location. Compensation for this position includes base salary and a performance-based bonus. The expected base salary for the role is $70,000 - $80,000. \n\nAdditional Considerations:\n\n - We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.\n\n - Interview Accommodations: Propel is committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the interview process. If you need accommodations due to a disability or medical condition (such as additional time or accessibility support), please let us know as early as possible so we can support you appropriately.\n\n - We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington.\n\n - Background Check Requirement: For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).\n\nMore About Propel\n\nPropel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like Vote.org, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly.\n\nPropel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.\n\nLearn more about our impact from the press\n\nFintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\nLate Show With Stephen Colbert http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\n\nHow to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\n\nHow Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share\n\nHow one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\n\nRecipients Affected By Government Shutdown https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\nHow hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\n\nJoin us, and let's build something amazing together!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d0e96770-a073-4d53-88b6-586d74db35e8","title":"Senior Full Stack Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"USA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[{"location":"Brooklyn, NYC","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"USA","addressLocality":"Brooklyn"}}}],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T19:30:01.968+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/d0e96770-a073-4d53-88b6-586d74db35e8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/d0e96770-a073-4d53-88b6-586d74db35e8/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Us</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel builds technology that strengthens the social safety net in America. We envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The safety net’s strength depends not just on funding, but delivery. Propel exists to dramatically improve how government benefits are delivered. Managing SNAP benefits, picking a D-SNP plan, or protecting against EBT theft should feel as seamless as Apple Pay or Netflix.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Governments struggle to build modern, scalable user experiences. We don’t.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Over 5.5 million Americans trust Propel today. We’ve grown revenue 35% YoY and are reinventing entire benefit categories, including Medicare, around the real needs of low-income Americans. We’re building a high-growth, high-ceiling, sustainable for-profit company where impact drives revenue.</p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re hiring a Senior Fullstack Engineer who wants to build consumer products at meaningful scale with real ownership.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is not a ticket-taking role. You’ll work across mobile apps, backend systems, internal tools, and new product lines. You’ll help identify problems, shape solutions, and ship iteratively in a space shaped by policy changes, evolving technology, and real-world constraints.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The technology landscape is evolving quickly, including the growing role of AI in how products are built and how users interact with technology. We don’t adopt trends blindly, but we do expect engineers to stay curious, experiment thoughtfully, and continuously evolve their craft as the world changes.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are not meeting-heavy. Engineers have meaningful heads-down time. Product, Design, and Engineering operate with shared values, curious, empathetic, user-first, which reduces friction and accelerates execution.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort with ambiguity, strong product instincts, and a bias toward action are essential.</p><h2><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and ship features across our mobile apps (Vue + TypeScript + Capacitor)<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop scalable backend systems (Python, Flask, Postgres, Redis, AWS)<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute to architecture and technical direction<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with Product and Design to scope and execute solutions<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Break ambiguous problems into iterative, shippable components<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Balance speed with long-term maintainability<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in on-call rotation<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Contribute through design reviews, code reviews, and mentorship<br /><br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will build systems used daily by millions of Americans to access food, healthcare, and financial stability.</p><h2><strong>What You Have</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years building and maintaining complex full-stack systems<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in startup or high-ambiguity environments<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong system design and product engineering fundamentals<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency in Python and JavaScript (or willingness to ramp quickly)<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Clear written and verbal communication skills<br /><br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mindset</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ownership: You take responsibility for outcomes<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Product Sense: You focus on solving the right problems<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Grit: You persist through ambiguity and setbacks<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curiosity: You think from first principles<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Urgency &amp; Accountability: You ask “why not now?”<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Low Ego: You step in where needed<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong Judgment: You prioritize effectively<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Iterative Mindset: You ship, learn, and improve<br /><br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Nice to have:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building consumer-scale applications<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with safety net programs (SNAP, WIC, TANF, SSI, SSDI, Medicaid, Section 8)<br /><br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$170,000 – $240,000 salary + meaningful equity<br />(Location-independent compensation)<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">20 Days PTO<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% 401K match<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$10k lifetime Carrot Fertility benefit<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent Medical, Dental, and Vision coverage<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote-first culture (NYC HQ)<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Monthly co-working stipend outside NYC<br /><br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We benchmark compensation around the 75th percentile and want your equity stake to matter long-term.</p><h2><strong>More About Propel and Our Engineering Team</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Technology is not a support function at Propel - it is the company.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe great tech companies:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solve user problems first<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build for scale and iteration<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Invest in quality and infrastructure<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stay curious about new technologies while exercising strong judgment<br /><br /></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We operate lean and transparently. You’ll understand our revenue drivers and big bets. Millions of users trust us and that responsibility is earned through consistently strong judgment.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’ve backed our mission with action:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Seeded emergency funds during government shutdowns<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Committed 1% of company equity into a user trust<br /><br /></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partnered carefully when sunsetting products to protect users<br /><br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Why This Role Might Not Be For You</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re building in the complex intersection of people, policy, and government systems. That work requires strong partnerships and comes with unique challenges.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We operate lean, and priorities can shift as policy, partners, or user needs evolve. Our environment isn’t highly structured with rigid swimlanes or long, predictable planning cycles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engineers move across product surfaces and problem spaces. This isn’t a narrowly scoped role focused on a single technical domain.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re building in an era where AI is reshaping team boundaries. Engineers here are comfortable contributing to product and design conversations, not just writing code.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We ship quickly while holding a high bar for quality and user trust. Balancing speed with thoughtful tradeoffs is part of the job.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our roadmap is influenced by legislation, regulatory changes, and evolving government systems. A certain level of external uncertainty is inherent to the space.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Career growth tends to come through ownership, impact, and stepping into stretch work rather than predefined ladders or timelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Technology evolves quickly, including AI. Staying curious and continuously evolving your craft is part of building a modern tech company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We value low-ego teammates who step in to help when something needs fixing, even if it falls outside a traditional lane.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are building a category-defining company in a complex space. That requires resilience, urgency, strong judgment, and a genuine desire to serve our users well.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If that energizes you - you’ll likely thrive here.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Considerations:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity in, which includes <strong>California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Background Check Requirement:</strong> For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Learn more about our impact from the press</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong>Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&amp;utm_medium=member_desktop&amp;rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\"><strong>Late Show With Stephen Colbert</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\"><strong>How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&amp;smid=sl-share\"><strong>How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\"><strong>How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong>Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown</strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\"><strong>How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond</strong></a></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Join us, and let's build something amazing together!</strong></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT US\n\nPropel builds technology that strengthens the social safety net in America. We envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.\n\nThe safety net’s strength depends not just on funding, but delivery. Propel exists to dramatically improve how government benefits are delivered. Managing SNAP benefits, picking a D-SNP plan, or protecting against EBT theft should feel as seamless as Apple Pay or Netflix.\n\nGovernments struggle to build modern, scalable user experiences. We don’t.\n\nOver 5.5 million Americans trust Propel today. We’ve grown revenue 35% YoY and are reinventing entire benefit categories, including Medicare, around the real needs of low-income Americans. We’re building a high-growth, high-ceiling, sustainable for-profit company where impact drives revenue.\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe’re hiring a Senior Fullstack Engineer who wants to build consumer products at meaningful scale with real ownership.\n\nThis is not a ticket-taking role. You’ll work across mobile apps, backend systems, internal tools, and new product lines. You’ll help identify problems, shape solutions, and ship iteratively in a space shaped by policy changes, evolving technology, and real-world constraints.\n\nThe technology landscape is evolving quickly, including the growing role of AI in how products are built and how users interact with technology. We don’t adopt trends blindly, but we do expect engineers to stay curious, experiment thoughtfully, and continuously evolve their craft as the world changes.\n\nWe are not meeting-heavy. Engineers have meaningful heads-down time. Product, Design, and Engineering operate with shared values, curious, empathetic, user-first, which reduces friction and accelerates execution.\n\nComfort with ambiguity, strong product instincts, and a bias toward action are essential.\n\n\nWHAT YOU’LL DO\n\n - Build and ship features across our mobile apps (Vue + TypeScript + Capacitor)\n   \n   \n\n - Develop scalable backend systems (Python, Flask, Postgres, Redis, AWS)\n   \n   \n\n - Contribute to architecture and technical direction\n   \n   \n\n - Partner closely with Product and Design to scope and execute solutions\n   \n   \n\n - Break ambiguous problems into iterative, shippable components\n   \n   \n\n - Balance speed with long-term maintainability\n   \n   \n\n - Participate in on-call rotation\n   \n   \n\n - Contribute through design reviews, code reviews, and mentorship\n   \n   \n\nYou will build systems used daily by millions of Americans to access food, healthcare, and financial stability.\n\n\nWHAT YOU HAVE\n\nExperience\n\n - 5+ years building and maintaining complex full-stack systems\n   \n   \n\n - Experience in startup or high-ambiguity environments\n   \n   \n\n - Strong system design and product engineering fundamentals\n   \n   \n\n - Fluency in Python and JavaScript (or willingness to ramp quickly)\n   \n   \n\n - Clear written and verbal communication skills\n   \n   \n\nMindset\n\n - Ownership: You take responsibility for outcomes\n   \n   \n\n - Product Sense: You focus on solving the right problems\n   \n   \n\n - Grit: You persist through ambiguity and setbacks\n   \n   \n\n - Curiosity: You think from first principles\n   \n   \n\n - Urgency & Accountability: You ask “why not now?”\n   \n   \n\n - Low Ego: You step in where needed\n   \n   \n\n - Strong Judgment: You prioritize effectively\n   \n   \n\n - Iterative Mindset: You ship, learn, and improve\n   \n   \n\nNice to have:\n\n - Experience building consumer-scale applications\n   \n   \n\n - Familiarity with safety net programs (SNAP, WIC, TANF, SSI, SSDI, Medicaid, Section 8)\n   \n   \n\n\nWHAT WE OFFER\n\n - $170,000 – $240,000 salary + meaningful equity\n   (Location-independent compensation)\n   \n   \n\n - 20 Days PTO\n   \n   \n\n - 4% 401K match\n   \n   \n\n - $10k lifetime Carrot Fertility benefit\n   \n   \n\n - Excellent Medical, Dental, and Vision coverage\n   \n   \n\n - Remote-first culture (NYC HQ)\n   \n   \n\n - Monthly co-working stipend outside NYC\n   \n   \n\nWe benchmark compensation around the 75th percentile and want your equity stake to matter long-term.\n\n\nMORE ABOUT PROPEL AND OUR ENGINEERING TEAM\n\nTechnology is not a support function at Propel - it is the company.\n\nWe believe great tech companies:\n\n - Solve user problems first\n   \n   \n\n - Build for scale and iteration\n   \n   \n\n - Invest in quality and infrastructure\n   \n   \n\n - Stay curious about new technologies while exercising strong judgment\n   \n   \n\nWe operate lean and transparently. You’ll understand our revenue drivers and big bets. Millions of users trust us and that responsibility is earned through consistently strong judgment.\n\nWe’ve backed our mission with action:\n\n - Seeded emergency funds during government shutdowns\n   \n   \n\n - Committed 1% of company equity into a user trust\n   \n   \n\n - Partnered carefully when sunsetting products to protect users\n   \n   \n\n\nWHY THIS ROLE MIGHT NOT BE FOR YOU\n\nWe’re building in the complex intersection of people, policy, and government systems. That work requires strong partnerships and comes with unique challenges.\n\n - We operate lean, and priorities can shift as policy, partners, or user needs evolve. Our environment isn’t highly structured with rigid swimlanes or long, predictable planning cycles.\n\n - Engineers move across product surfaces and problem spaces. This isn’t a narrowly scoped role focused on a single technical domain.\n\n - We’re building in an era where AI is reshaping team boundaries. Engineers here are comfortable contributing to product and design conversations, not just writing code.\n\n - We ship quickly while holding a high bar for quality and user trust. Balancing speed with thoughtful tradeoffs is part of the job.\n\n - Our roadmap is influenced by legislation, regulatory changes, and evolving government systems. A certain level of external uncertainty is inherent to the space.\n\n - Career growth tends to come through ownership, impact, and stepping into stretch work rather than predefined ladders or timelines.\n\n - Technology evolves quickly, including AI. Staying curious and continuously evolving your craft is part of building a modern tech company.\n\n - We value low-ego teammates who step in to help when something needs fixing, even if it falls outside a traditional lane.\n\n - We are building a category-defining company in a complex space. That requires resilience, urgency, strong judgment, and a genuine desire to serve our users well.\n\nIf that energizes you - you’ll likely thrive here.\n\nAdditional Considerations:\n\n - We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.\n\n - We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity in, which includes California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington.\n\n - Background Check Requirement: For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).\n\nLearn more about our impact from the press\n\n - Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - Late Show With Stephen Colbert http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\n\n - How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\n\n - How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share\n\n - How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\n\n - Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\n\nJoin us, and let's build something amazing together!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b92d010e-7806-4927-8062-3d1244d1f4e5","title":"Senior Solutions Architect, Government Partnerships","department":"Public Partnerships and Policy","team":"Public Partnerships and Policy","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"USA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-04-09T21:19:48.006+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/b92d010e-7806-4927-8062-3d1244d1f4e5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/b92d010e-7806-4927-8062-3d1244d1f4e5/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is on a mission to empower low-income Americans by simplifying access to government benefits with modern technology. We're a passionate team of 100 Propellers - all working to help our users get through the month, every month.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a Solutions Architect to bridge Propel's Government Partnerships team and our Product &amp; Engineering organization - translating state partners' needs into product strategy, and then owning the delivery of that work with states. This role has the opportunity to shape the way our product evolves with deeper government partnerships and increase the value we’re able to deliver to both users and government partners.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>This is a hands-on IC role.</strong> You'll be the person writing the scoping doc, building the dashboard, sitting in the state meeting, configuring the campaign, and running the evaluation. You own both strategy and execution end to end. Over time, as this work scales, the role has potential to grow into a leadership position — but today we need someone who is excited about the execution.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll work across the state partnership funnel, from early relationship-building through campaign delivery. You should be the kind of person who can walk into a meeting with a state SNAP agency, understand their operational pain points around payment error rates or portal access, walk out with a concrete plan that maps to Propel's product roadmap — and then go execute it. The role reports into our Government Partnerships team, with a dotted line to Product.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Here's how you'll impact the company:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Be the product voice in state conversations.</strong> Prepare materials, present Propel's capabilities, and field technical questions from state partners directly. Translate what you learn into structured requirements and recommendations for product and engineering.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own state campaign delivery end to end.</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"> Define what Propel will deliver for each state engagement, write the scope-of-work, set up campaign infrastructure, monitor execution, run the evaluation, and fix what breaks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lean into AI-enablement to create more leverage for our partnerships work with less engineering support.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Make hands-on tradeoff decisions about when a state's needs warrant new product investment vs. existing capabilities — and when it's configuration work, do it yourself.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Feed the case management product roadmap.</strong> Synthesize patterns across engagements to surface common needs and platform gaps. Bring specific, evidence-based recommendations to PMs — not just \"states want X,\" but \"here's the pattern across three states, here's what a platform-level solution looks like, and here's the data.\"</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You Might Be a Great Fit If You Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>5+ years bridging product/technical teams and external partners</strong> — solutions architecture, implementation/delivery leadership, technical program management, or product management in a B2G context. You should have direct experience working in or selling to state SNAP or Medicaid agencies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical background – </strong>you’re comfortable getting in the weeds on how our tech stack operates to tackle questions around how we should integrate with state partners. You are comfortable reading API docs, translating technical documents for non-technical stakeholders and doing a first-draft estimate of complexity and scope for new tasks.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Familiarity with public benefits administration</strong> — SNAP, Medicaid, EBT, or adjacent programs. You understand (or can quickly learn) how state agencies work, what their incentives are, and why things like payment error rates and redetermination processes matter</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The ability to operate across altitudes</strong> — presenting to a state CIO on Monday, speccing a campaign config on Tuesday, analyzing pilot results on Wednesday, drafting a SOW on Thursday</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong product instincts</strong> — you can tell the difference between a state request that should become a platform feature and one that should stay a one-off. You know when to advocate for one-off investments because they are critical to the state pipeline, and when they should be left on the table.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Comfort with ambiguity</strong> — we're inventing a new model for how a consumer tech company partners with state agencies, and you'll be building the plane while flying it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Communication and data skills</strong> — clear writing, compelling decks, and enough SQL/analytics fluency to tell the story of a campaign's impact</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Bonus Points</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in case management systems, benefits administration tech, or health plan operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Previous experience as an engineer or technical PM</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with program evaluation — defining success metrics, measurement frameworks, and presenting results to government stakeholders</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Propel, you'll enjoy:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote-friendly work environment with a dog-friendly office in Downtown Brooklyn. The team meets in-person for optional retreats.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">20 Days of PTO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% 401K match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A strong equity package that reflects the leveling and anticipated impact of this role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fair, equitable, and competitive salaries. Propel believes that everyone should be compensated fairly and equitably. We set our salary ranges using compensation data from hundreds of NYC based startups at our stage. Additionally, pay is not determined based on location. The salary range for this position is <strong>$160,000 - $190,000</strong> depending on experience and interview performance. Equity and excellent benefits come with this position as well!</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Considerations:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interview Accommodations:</strong> Propel is committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the interview process. If you need accommodations due to a disability or medical condition (such as additional time or accessibility support), please let us know as early as possible so we can support you appropriately.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes <strong>California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Background Check Requirement:</strong> For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>More About Propel</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Vote.org\">Vote.org</a>, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Learn more about our impact from the press</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong><u>Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&amp;utm_medium=member_desktop&amp;rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\"><strong><u>Late Show With Stephen Colbert</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\"><strong><u>How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&amp;smid=sl-share\"><strong><u>How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\"><strong><u>How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong><u>Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\"><strong><u>How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond</u></strong></a></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Join us, and let's build something amazing together!</strong></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us\n\nPropel is on a mission to empower low-income Americans by simplifying access to government benefits with modern technology. We're a passionate team of 100 Propellers - all working to help our users get through the month, every month.\n\n\n\nAbout the Role\n\nWe're looking for a Solutions Architect to bridge Propel's Government Partnerships team and our Product & Engineering organization - translating state partners' needs into product strategy, and then owning the delivery of that work with states. This role has the opportunity to shape the way our product evolves with deeper government partnerships and increase the value we’re able to deliver to both users and government partners.\n\nThis is a hands-on IC role. You'll be the person writing the scoping doc, building the dashboard, sitting in the state meeting, configuring the campaign, and running the evaluation. You own both strategy and execution end to end. Over time, as this work scales, the role has potential to grow into a leadership position — but today we need someone who is excited about the execution.\n\nYou'll work across the state partnership funnel, from early relationship-building through campaign delivery. You should be the kind of person who can walk into a meeting with a state SNAP agency, understand their operational pain points around payment error rates or portal access, walk out with a concrete plan that maps to Propel's product roadmap — and then go execute it. The role reports into our Government Partnerships team, with a dotted line to Product.\n\n\n\nHere's how you'll impact the company:\n\n - Be the product voice in state conversations. Prepare materials, present Propel's capabilities, and field technical questions from state partners directly. Translate what you learn into structured requirements and recommendations for product and engineering.\n\n - Own state campaign delivery end to end.\n   \n   -  Define what Propel will deliver for each state engagement, write the scope-of-work, set up campaign infrastructure, monitor execution, run the evaluation, and fix what breaks.\n   \n   - Lean into AI-enablement to create more leverage for our partnerships work with less engineering support.\n   \n   - Make hands-on tradeoff decisions about when a state's needs warrant new product investment vs. existing capabilities — and when it's configuration work, do it yourself.\n\n - Feed the case management product roadmap. Synthesize patterns across engagements to surface common needs and platform gaps. Bring specific, evidence-based recommendations to PMs — not just \"states want X,\" but \"here's the pattern across three states, here's what a platform-level solution looks like, and here's the data.\"\n\n\n\nYou Might Be a Great Fit If You Have\n\n - 5+ years bridging product/technical teams and external partners — solutions architecture, implementation/delivery leadership, technical program management, or product management in a B2G context. You should have direct experience working in or selling to state SNAP or Medicaid agencies.\n\n - Technical background – you’re comfortable getting in the weeds on how our tech stack operates to tackle questions around how we should integrate with state partners. You are comfortable reading API docs, translating technical documents for non-technical stakeholders and doing a first-draft estimate of complexity and scope for new tasks.\n\n - Familiarity with public benefits administration — SNAP, Medicaid, EBT, or adjacent programs. You understand (or can quickly learn) how state agencies work, what their incentives are, and why things like payment error rates and redetermination processes matter\n\n - The ability to operate across altitudes — presenting to a state CIO on Monday, speccing a campaign config on Tuesday, analyzing pilot results on Wednesday, drafting a SOW on Thursday\n\n - Strong product instincts — you can tell the difference between a state request that should become a platform feature and one that should stay a one-off. You know when to advocate for one-off investments because they are critical to the state pipeline, and when they should be left on the table.\n\n - Comfort with ambiguity — we're inventing a new model for how a consumer tech company partners with state agencies, and you'll be building the plane while flying it\n\n - Communication and data skills — clear writing, compelling decks, and enough SQL/analytics fluency to tell the story of a campaign's impact\n\nBonus Points\n\n - Background in case management systems, benefits administration tech, or health plan operations\n\n - Previous experience as an engineer or technical PM\n\n - Experience with program evaluation — defining success metrics, measurement frameworks, and presenting results to government stakeholders\n\n\n\nAt Propel, you'll enjoy:\n\n - Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission\n\n - Remote-friendly work environment with a dog-friendly office in Downtown Brooklyn. The team meets in-person for optional retreats.\n\n - 20 Days of PTO\n\n - 4% 401K match\n\n - $10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility\n\n - Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options\n\n - A strong equity package that reflects the leveling and anticipated impact of this role\n\n - Fair, equitable, and competitive salaries. Propel believes that everyone should be compensated fairly and equitably. We set our salary ranges using compensation data from hundreds of NYC based startups at our stage. Additionally, pay is not determined based on location. The salary range for this position is $160,000 - $190,000 depending on experience and interview performance. Equity and excellent benefits come with this position as well!\n\nAdditional Considerations:\n\n - We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.\n\n - Interview Accommodations: Propel is committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the interview process. If you need accommodations due to a disability or medical condition (such as additional time or accessibility support), please let us know as early as possible so we can support you appropriately.\n\n - We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington.\n\n - Background Check Requirement: For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).\n   \n   \n\nMore About Propel\n\nPropel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like Vote.org http://Vote.org, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly.\n\nPropel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.\n\nLearn more about our impact from the press\n\n - Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - Late Show With Stephen Colbert http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\n\n - How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\n\n - How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share\n\n - How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\n\n - Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\n\nJoin us, and let's build something amazing together!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$160K – $190K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$160K - $190K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"542cbd4c-0461-473b-a405-40347a1272d2","tierSummary":"Base Salary $160K – $190K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"99450b30-152a-4110-8d19-4a0da8821497","summary":"Base Salary $160K – $190K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":190000},{"id":"8d3042e8-0938-4466-acc7-8a73550dbf11","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":190000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"398e2439-ad4a-4c84-a295-27ebda92c34f","title":"GTM Strategy & Operations Lead","department":"Ads Marketplace","team":"Ads Marketplace","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"USA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-01T22:30:46.245+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/398e2439-ad4a-4c84-a295-27ebda92c34f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/398e2439-ad4a-4c84-a295-27ebda92c34f/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is on a mission to empower low-income Americans by simplifying access to government benefits with modern technology. We're a passionate team of 100 Propellers - all working to help our users get through the month, every month.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We launched the Propel Marketplace to connect our ~5M monthly active users to products, services, and exclusive offers from leading brands across grocery and retail, healthcare, telecoms, financial services, and auto. It has grown into a powerful, industry-leading performance tool for our partners and a critical revenue driver for Propel. We have strong product market fit, our users love our app, and our customers love that we have a significant reach and engagement with our users.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a <strong>GTM Strategy and Operations Lead</strong>! We're scaling revenue operations for a profitable marketplace - and we need someone who moves fast, thinks strategically, and is eager to provide proactive support to senior leaders.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll own the RevOps program end-to-end: embedding AI into our tech stack, surfacing insights that drive decisions, and serving as a trusted partner to the Customer Success and Business Development teams. You stay ahead of industry trends and hold yourself to a high bar.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-visibility role on our Marketplace Strategy &amp; Operations team, reporting to the Director of Strategy &amp; Operations. You’ll work closely with the GM of Marketplace, Head of CS, and Head of BD &amp; Sales.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Here's how you'll impact the company</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Power GTM planning: </strong>Lead comp planning and goal-setting in partnership with Sales, CS, and the GM as we push toward our next growth milestone</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Drive analytical rigor: </strong>Diagnose performance gaps with hypothesis-driven analysis, build dashboards that surface what actually matters, and make actionable recommendations based on your findings</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Own the GTM tech stack: </strong>Serve as our primary Salesforce admin and own the broader suite of tools that Sales and CS rely on - maintaining data integrity, driving adoption, and proactively identifying new tools (including AI-powered ones) that make the team more effective</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Enable the team: </strong>Build processes that stick, standardize how we work across BD and CS, and establish AI usage guidelines that ensure consistency across team outputs so the team can move fast without creating fragmentation</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience: </strong>3+ years in analytical roles supporting enterprise GTM teams (BizOps, Revenue Operations, Revenue Enablement, etc.). Experience at growth stage company (50-200 employees) strongly preferred</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Analytical rigor: </strong>You take a hypothesis-driven approach, know how to frame a question well, and deliver findings with clear logic and a point of view</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Self-directed: </strong>Comfortable prioritizing in an ambiguous environment and picking up new tools and contexts quickly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI fluency: </strong>You proactively explore ways to use AI tools to improve team workflows and GTM processes. You know when and where to use them to accelerate great judgment, not just to move faster</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Documentation:</strong> Your materials are self-explanatory, well-structured, and formatted for the audience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>GTM tech stack: </strong>Must be comfortable with or willing to learn and own Salesforce - building, maintaining, and improving the instance. Knowledge and curiosity for other GTM tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience in ads, ad tech, or performance marketing is a plus</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Propel, you'll enjoy</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote-friendly work environment with a dog-friendly office in Downtown Brooklyn. The team meets in-person for optional retreats.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">20 Days of PTO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% 401K match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Other health and mental health focused benefits and perks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel believes that everyone should be compensated fairly and equitably. We set our salary ranges using compensation data from hundreds of NYC-based startups at our stage. Additionally, pay is not determined based on location. Compensation for this position includes base salary and a performance-based bonus. The bonus is a combination of individual and team revenue performance. Depending on experience, this role will be filled at one of two levels:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>GTM Strategy and Ops Lead:</strong> The expected base salary is <strong>$120,000 - $160,000</strong>, with a <strong>total on-target earnings (OTE) of $132,000 - $176,000</strong>.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Equity and excellent benefits come with this position as well!</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Considerations:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interview Accommodations:</strong> Propel is committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the interview process. If you need accommodations due to a disability or medical condition (such as additional time or accessibility support), please let us know as early as possible so we can support you appropriately.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes <strong>California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Background Check Requirement:</strong> For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>More About Propel</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Vote.org\">Vote.org</a>, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Learn more about our impact from the press</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong><u>Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&amp;utm_medium=member_desktop&amp;rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\"><strong><u>Late Show With Stephen Colbert</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\"><strong><u>How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&amp;smid=sl-share\"><strong><u>How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/jeffkauflin/2020/04/03/fintech-apps-offer-first-aid-for-hardest-hit-consumers/#70df70611a93\"><strong><u>Propel Routes Money to those Who Need it Most</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\"><strong><u>How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong><u>Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\"><strong><u>How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.joinpropel.com/covid-19\"><strong><u>Helping our Users Navigate this Crisis</u></strong></a></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Join us, and let's build something amazing together!</strong></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us\n\nPropel is on a mission to empower low-income Americans by simplifying access to government benefits with modern technology. We're a passionate team of 100 Propellers - all working to help our users get through the month, every month.\n\nThe Role\n\nWe launched the Propel Marketplace to connect our ~5M monthly active users to products, services, and exclusive offers from leading brands across grocery and retail, healthcare, telecoms, financial services, and auto. It has grown into a powerful, industry-leading performance tool for our partners and a critical revenue driver for Propel. We have strong product market fit, our users love our app, and our customers love that we have a significant reach and engagement with our users.\n\nWe’re looking for a GTM Strategy and Operations Lead! We're scaling revenue operations for a profitable marketplace - and we need someone who moves fast, thinks strategically, and is eager to provide proactive support to senior leaders.\n\nYou'll own the RevOps program end-to-end: embedding AI into our tech stack, surfacing insights that drive decisions, and serving as a trusted partner to the Customer Success and Business Development teams. You stay ahead of industry trends and hold yourself to a high bar.\n\nThis is a high-visibility role on our Marketplace Strategy & Operations team, reporting to the Director of Strategy & Operations. You’ll work closely with the GM of Marketplace, Head of CS, and Head of BD & Sales.\n\nHere's how you'll impact the company\n\n - Power GTM planning: Lead comp planning and goal-setting in partnership with Sales, CS, and the GM as we push toward our next growth milestone\n\n - Drive analytical rigor: Diagnose performance gaps with hypothesis-driven analysis, build dashboards that surface what actually matters, and make actionable recommendations based on your findings\n\n - Own the GTM tech stack: Serve as our primary Salesforce admin and own the broader suite of tools that Sales and CS rely on - maintaining data integrity, driving adoption, and proactively identifying new tools (including AI-powered ones) that make the team more effective\n\n - Enable the team: Build processes that stick, standardize how we work across BD and CS, and establish AI usage guidelines that ensure consistency across team outputs so the team can move fast without creating fragmentation\n\nRequirements\n\n - Experience: 3+ years in analytical roles supporting enterprise GTM teams (BizOps, Revenue Operations, Revenue Enablement, etc.). Experience at growth stage company (50-200 employees) strongly preferred\n\n - Analytical rigor: You take a hypothesis-driven approach, know how to frame a question well, and deliver findings with clear logic and a point of view\n\n - Self-directed: Comfortable prioritizing in an ambiguous environment and picking up new tools and contexts quickly\n\n - AI fluency: You proactively explore ways to use AI tools to improve team workflows and GTM processes. You know when and where to use them to accelerate great judgment, not just to move faster\n\n - Documentation: Your materials are self-explanatory, well-structured, and formatted for the audience\n\n - GTM tech stack: Must be comfortable with or willing to learn and own Salesforce - building, maintaining, and improving the instance. Knowledge and curiosity for other GTM tools\n\n - Experience in ads, ad tech, or performance marketing is a plus\n\nAt Propel, you'll enjoy\n\n - Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission\n\n - Remote-friendly work environment with a dog-friendly office in Downtown Brooklyn. The team meets in-person for optional retreats.\n\n - 20 Days of PTO\n\n - 4% 401K match\n\n - $10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility\n\n - Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options\n\n - Other health and mental health focused benefits and perks\n\n - Propel believes that everyone should be compensated fairly and equitably. We set our salary ranges using compensation data from hundreds of NYC-based startups at our stage. Additionally, pay is not determined based on location. Compensation for this position includes base salary and a performance-based bonus. The bonus is a combination of individual and team revenue performance. Depending on experience, this role will be filled at one of two levels:\n   \n   - GTM Strategy and Ops Lead: The expected base salary is $120,000 - $160,000, with a total on-target earnings (OTE) of $132,000 - $176,000.\n   \n   Equity and excellent benefits come with this position as well!\n\nAdditional Considerations:\n\n - We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.\n\n - Interview Accommodations: Propel is committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the interview process. If you need accommodations due to a disability or medical condition (such as additional time or accessibility support), please let us know as early as possible so we can support you appropriately.\n\n - We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington.\n\n - Background Check Requirement: For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).\n\nMore About Propel\n\nPropel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like Vote.org http://Vote.org, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly.\n\nPropel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.\n\nLearn more about our impact from the press\n\n - Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - Late Show With Stephen Colbert http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\n\n - How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\n\n - How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share\n\n - Propel Routes Money to those Who Need it Most https://www.forbes.com/sites/jeffkauflin/2020/04/03/fintech-apps-offer-first-aid-for-hardest-hit-consumers/#70df70611a93\n\n - How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\n\n - Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\n\n - Helping our Users Navigate this Crisis https://www.joinpropel.com/covid-19\n\nJoin us, and let's build something amazing together!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$120K – $160K • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$120K - $160K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"0d4caa4a-9229-4e78-b273-e650d679ac2b","tierSummary":"Base Salary $120K – $160K • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"6f95f937-e892-4917-9cc5-f0cdab8adfa8","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"4a3a3c15-76c5-4f32-bf14-6242c7013a84","summary":"Base Salary $120K – $160K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":160000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":120000,"maxValue":160000}]}},{"id":"fa7ca24a-e80e-4706-982f-82a3f058776a","title":"Product Lead, Grocery","department":"Product","team":"Product","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"USA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-12T21:48:10.948+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/fa7ca24a-e80e-4706-982f-82a3f058776a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/fa7ca24a-e80e-4706-982f-82a3f058776a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Propel</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is on a mission to build technology that strengthens the social safety net. We’re a passionate team of ~100 Propellers who envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We launched the Propel Marketplace to connect our ~5M monthly active users to products, services, and exclusive offers from leading brands across grocery and retail, healthcare, telecoms, financial services, and auto. It has grown into a powerful, industry-leading performance tool for our partners and a critical revenue driver for Propel. We have strong product market fit, our users love our app, and our customers love that we have a significant reach and engagement with our users.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're hiring a <strong>Product Lead (Senior or Staff Product Manager)</strong> to own the Grocery product vertical that sits within our broader Marketplace product ecosystem. You'll inherit and drive a large cross-functional team (engineers, designers, and data scientists) with a clear problem space and momentum. In addition to running a cross-functional product squad, you'll partner closely with our business team across business development and customer success. You’ll report directly to the VP of Product.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for someone who is an excellent executor and is excited to drive user and commercial strategy. You'll ship — fast, with quality, across a tight cross functional pod — and you'll also shape the bets: which user segments we build for, how we translate retailer and CPG demand into a product users love, and where the durable value (and revenue) actually comes from. We’re looking for someone who is excited and energized by the opportunity to balance commercial strategy with low income user experiences.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What you'll do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own the end-to-end product vision &amp; strategy for grocery – both how we help users save money on groceries and how we create value for commercial partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deeply understand the grocery shopping habits &amp; needs of SNAP recipients &amp; be able to identify areas of opportunity &amp; overlap with retailers &amp; CPGs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Balance a portfolio of smaller experiments and larger 0 →1 efforts that define our roadmap in the space – this looks like sharp hypothesis definition, fast iteration and close collaboration with engineering, design &amp; sales</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define &amp; track the success metrics that tie user value to commercial performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate product strategy clearly to leadership, cross-functional teams and commercial partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Uses AI tools (we use Claude) fluently to move faster - turning a rough brief into a structured doc, a messy transcript into clear action items, or a vague ask into a scoped problem statement</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of product management experience with direct experience shipping large-scale consumer products</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Commercial fluency &amp; partnership experience.</strong> You’ve had to work with commercial partners before (ideally in the retail space), and gone through the exercise of identifying areas of overlap in user and partner needs. You can sit across the table from a retailer or CPG, understand what they need, and translate requirements into the product — without losing sight of user value.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Demonstrated 0→1 product experience.</strong> You’ve taken a product from an idea or early concept to a shipped, scaled solution.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI fluency.</strong> You use AI tools fluently as part of daily work - prompting effectively, evaluating outputs critically, and applying them where they genuinely accelerate the work, whether that's synthesizing research, structuring docs, or turning ambiguous asks into scoped problem statements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Data-driven.</strong> You reach for the data yourself (we run on Amplitude, Metabase/Snowflake), frame the right metrics, and can tell the difference between a real signal and a vanity one.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Mission-aligned. </strong>You care about building for low-income and underserved users, and you bring both empathy and rigor to it. You hold a high bar that behavior change has to be worth it for the user, even when there's no revenue upside.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Startup experience.</strong> You’re comfortable with ambiguity, move fast, and know how to make smart tradeoffs with limited resources.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Exceptional communication skills.</strong> you can present a product vision to a C-suite buyer and write a clear PRD with equal confidence.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong collaboration skills</strong> with both technical and non-technical stakeholders</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Propel, you'll enjoy</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote-friendly work environment with a dog-friendly office in Downtown Brooklyn. The team meets in-person for optional retreats.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">20 Days of PTO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% 401K match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Other health and mental health focused benefits and perks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel believes that everyone should be compensated fairly and equitably. We set our salary ranges using compensation data from hundreds of NYC-based startups at our stage. Additionally, pay is not determined based on location. The expected base salary for the role is <strong>$190,000 - $250,000</strong>. Equity and excellent benefits come with this position as well!</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Considerations:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Interview Accommodations:</strong> Propel is committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the interview process. If you need accommodations due to a disability or medical condition (such as additional time or accessibility support), please let us know as early as possible so we can support you appropriately.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes <strong>California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Background Check Requirement:</strong> For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>More About Propel</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Vote.org\">Vote.org</a>, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Learn more about our impact from the press</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong><u>Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&amp;utm_medium=member_desktop&amp;rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\"><strong><u>Late Show With Stephen Colbert</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\"><strong><u>How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&amp;smid=sl-share\"><strong><u>How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/jeffkauflin/2020/04/03/fintech-apps-offer-first-aid-for-hardest-hit-consumers/#70df70611a93\"><strong><u>Propel Routes Money to those Who Need it Most</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\"><strong><u>How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong><u>Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\"><strong><u>How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.joinpropel.com/covid-19\"><strong><u>Helping our Users Navigate this Crisis</u></strong></a></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Join us, and let's build something amazing together!</strong></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT PROPEL\n\nPropel is on a mission to build technology that strengthens the social safety net. We’re a passionate team of ~100 Propellers who envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe launched the Propel Marketplace to connect our ~5M monthly active users to products, services, and exclusive offers from leading brands across grocery and retail, healthcare, telecoms, financial services, and auto. It has grown into a powerful, industry-leading performance tool for our partners and a critical revenue driver for Propel. We have strong product market fit, our users love our app, and our customers love that we have a significant reach and engagement with our users.\n\nWe're hiring a Product Lead (Senior or Staff Product Manager) to own the Grocery product vertical that sits within our broader Marketplace product ecosystem. You'll inherit and drive a large cross-functional team (engineers, designers, and data scientists) with a clear problem space and momentum. In addition to running a cross-functional product squad, you'll partner closely with our business team across business development and customer success. You’ll report directly to the VP of Product.\n\nWe’re looking for someone who is an excellent executor and is excited to drive user and commercial strategy. You'll ship — fast, with quality, across a tight cross functional pod — and you'll also shape the bets: which user segments we build for, how we translate retailer and CPG demand into a product users love, and where the durable value (and revenue) actually comes from. We’re looking for someone who is excited and energized by the opportunity to balance commercial strategy with low income user experiences.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own the end-to-end product vision & strategy for grocery – both how we help users save money on groceries and how we create value for commercial partners\n\n - Deeply understand the grocery shopping habits & needs of SNAP recipients & be able to identify areas of opportunity & overlap with retailers & CPGs\n\n - Balance a portfolio of smaller experiments and larger 0 →1 efforts that define our roadmap in the space – this looks like sharp hypothesis definition, fast iteration and close collaboration with engineering, design & sales\n\n - Define & track the success metrics that tie user value to commercial performance\n\n - Communicate product strategy clearly to leadership, cross-functional teams and commercial partners\n\n - Uses AI tools (we use Claude) fluently to move faster - turning a rough brief into a structured doc, a messy transcript into clear action items, or a vague ask into a scoped problem statement\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 5+ years of product management experience with direct experience shipping large-scale consumer products\n\n - Commercial fluency & partnership experience. You’ve had to work with commercial partners before (ideally in the retail space), and gone through the exercise of identifying areas of overlap in user and partner needs. You can sit across the table from a retailer or CPG, understand what they need, and translate requirements into the product — without losing sight of user value.\n\n - Demonstrated 0→1 product experience. You’ve taken a product from an idea or early concept to a shipped, scaled solution.\n\n - AI fluency. You use AI tools fluently as part of daily work - prompting effectively, evaluating outputs critically, and applying them where they genuinely accelerate the work, whether that's synthesizing research, structuring docs, or turning ambiguous asks into scoped problem statements.\n\n - Data-driven. You reach for the data yourself (we run on Amplitude, Metabase/Snowflake), frame the right metrics, and can tell the difference between a real signal and a vanity one.\n\n - Mission-aligned. You care about building for low-income and underserved users, and you bring both empathy and rigor to it. You hold a high bar that behavior change has to be worth it for the user, even when there's no revenue upside.\n\n - Startup experience. You’re comfortable with ambiguity, move fast, and know how to make smart tradeoffs with limited resources.\n\n - Exceptional communication skills. you can present a product vision to a C-suite buyer and write a clear PRD with equal confidence.\n\n - Strong collaboration skills with both technical and non-technical stakeholders\n\nAt Propel, you'll enjoy\n\n - Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission\n\n - Remote-friendly work environment with a dog-friendly office in Downtown Brooklyn. The team meets in-person for optional retreats.\n\n - 20 Days of PTO\n\n - 4% 401K match\n\n - $10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility\n\n - Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options\n\n - Other health and mental health focused benefits and perks\n\n - Propel believes that everyone should be compensated fairly and equitably. We set our salary ranges using compensation data from hundreds of NYC-based startups at our stage. Additionally, pay is not determined based on location. The expected base salary for the role is $190,000 - $250,000. Equity and excellent benefits come with this position as well!\n\nAdditional Considerations:\n\n - We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.\n\n - Interview Accommodations: Propel is committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the interview process. If you need accommodations due to a disability or medical condition (such as additional time or accessibility support), please let us know as early as possible so we can support you appropriately.\n\n - We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington.\n\n - Background Check Requirement: For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).\n\nMore About Propel\n\nPropel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like Vote.org http://Vote.org, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly.\n\nPropel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.\n\nLearn more about our impact from the press\n\n - Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - Late Show With Stephen Colbert http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\n\n - How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\n\n - How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share\n\n - Propel Routes Money to those Who Need it Most https://www.forbes.com/sites/jeffkauflin/2020/04/03/fintech-apps-offer-first-aid-for-hardest-hit-consumers/#70df70611a93\n\n - How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\n\n - Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\n\n - Helping our Users Navigate this Crisis https://www.joinpropel.com/covid-19\n\nJoin us, and let's build something amazing together!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$190K – $250K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$190K - $250K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"80df79f6-f1af-45e9-8de9-5bd35c45ad76","tierSummary":"$190K – $250K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"c470a0c5-5f6c-4620-8718-bcb47b1606b2","summary":"$190K – $250K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":190000,"maxValue":250000},{"id":"59a2bdd0-af3c-474c-8198-174f75b9998e","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":190000,"maxValue":250000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"0bc0101a-f096-4f46-a7d7-cf812221ee0f","title":"Product Marketing Manager","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"USA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T14:47:34.330+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/0bc0101a-f096-4f46-a7d7-cf812221ee0f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/0bc0101a-f096-4f46-a7d7-cf812221ee0f/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel builds technology that strengthens the social safety net in America. We envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The safety net’s strength depends not just on funding, but delivery. Propel exists to dramatically improve how government benefits are delivered. Managing SNAP benefits, picking a D-SNP plan, or protecting against EBT theft should feel as seamless as Apple Pay or Netflix.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Governments struggle to build modern, scalable user experiences. We don’t.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Over 5 million Americans trust Propel today. We’ve grown revenue 35% YoY and are reinventing entire benefit categories, including Medicare, around the real needs of low-income Americans. We’re building a high-growth, high-ceiling, sustainable for-profit company where impact drives revenue.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is launching new products that expand how we help people save money and access essential services. We’re looking for a Product Marketing Manager to help bring these products to market and grow their reach.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role will focus on consumer products and features that connect SNAP recipients with ways to save on everyday essentials and access healthcare—from grocery and retail offers to tools that help people navigate Medicare coverage. You’ll develop positioning and messaging, shape go-to-market and ongoing marketing strategies, and partner closely with Product, Lifecycle, Growth, Research, and business leads to drive adoption and repeat engagement. You’ll report to the Director of Product Marketing.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a deep understanding of our audiences—their needs, motivations, perceptions, and sources of confusion—and use those insights to shape product and marketing decisions.</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define and test differentiated positioning, value propositions, naming, and messaging.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write clear, compelling customer-facing copy for product launches and lifecycle communications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Lead go-to-market and lifecycle plans that drive discovery, activation, and repeat engagement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bring audience and market insight into product development, from early strategy through launch and iteration.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Define success measures, design experiments, and use adoption, engagement, conversion, and revenue data to evaluate impact and adjust the strategy.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience in product marketing or a closely related role, ideally in a consumer technology environment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional writing skills and the ability to make complex products clear, compelling, and trustworthy.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of developing positioning and messaging and leading go-to-market strategy for new or evolving products.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience writing lifecycle communications that support onboarding, engagement, retention, or reactivation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong audience orientation and a practical approach to using qualitative and quantitative insights to make decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of setting measurable goals, designing experiments, and using adoption, engagement, conversion, and revenue data to evaluate impact.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort operating autonomously in a fast-moving environment, creating structure from ambiguity, adapting as priorities shift, and building buy-in across teams.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Especially Helpful</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience marketing products in benefits, healthcare, Medicare, financial technology, or another complex or highly regulated consumer category.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Propel, you'll enjoy:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote-friendly work environment with a dog-friendly office in Downtown Brooklyn. The team meets in-person for optional retreats a few times per year.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">20 Days of PTO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% 401K match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Other health and mental health focused benefits and perks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel builds compensation bands referencing the 75th percentile of compensation for companies like us. <em>Expected</em> compensation for the role as scoped is $125,000 - $175,000 and will be based on how a candidate matches to our internal leveling guide.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Considerations:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes <strong>California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Background Check Requirement:</strong> For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>More About Propel</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Vote.org\">Vote.org</a>, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors, including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Learn more about our impact from the press</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong><u>Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&amp;utm_medium=member_desktop&amp;rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\"><strong><u>Late Show With Stephen Colbert</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\"><strong><u>How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&amp;smid=sl-share\"><strong><u>How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/jeffkauflin/2020/04/03/fintech-apps-offer-first-aid-for-hardest-hit-consumers/#70df70611a93\"><strong><u>Propel Routes Money to those Who Need it Most</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\"><strong><u>How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\"><strong><u>Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\"><strong><u>How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond</u></strong></a></p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.joinpropel.com/covid-19\"><strong><u>Helping our Users Navigate this Crisis</u></strong></a></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Join us, and let's build something amazing together!</strong></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Us\n\nPropel builds technology that strengthens the social safety net in America. We envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.\n\nThe safety net’s strength depends not just on funding, but delivery. Propel exists to dramatically improve how government benefits are delivered. Managing SNAP benefits, picking a D-SNP plan, or protecting against EBT theft should feel as seamless as Apple Pay or Netflix.\n\nGovernments struggle to build modern, scalable user experiences. We don’t.\n\nOver 5 million Americans trust Propel today. We’ve grown revenue 35% YoY and are reinventing entire benefit categories, including Medicare, around the real needs of low-income Americans. We’re building a high-growth, high-ceiling, sustainable for-profit company where impact drives revenue.\n\nThe Role\n\nPropel is launching new products that expand how we help people save money and access essential services. We’re looking for a Product Marketing Manager to help bring these products to market and grow their reach.\n\nThis role will focus on consumer products and features that connect SNAP recipients with ways to save on everyday essentials and access healthcare—from grocery and retail offers to tools that help people navigate Medicare coverage. You’ll develop positioning and messaging, shape go-to-market and ongoing marketing strategies, and partner closely with Product, Lifecycle, Growth, Research, and business leads to drive adoption and repeat engagement. You’ll report to the Director of Product Marketing.\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\n - Build a deep understanding of our audiences—their needs, motivations, perceptions, and sources of confusion—and use those insights to shape product and marketing decisions.\n\n - Define and test differentiated positioning, value propositions, naming, and messaging.\n\n - Write clear, compelling customer-facing copy for product launches and lifecycle communications.\n\n - Lead go-to-market and lifecycle plans that drive discovery, activation, and repeat engagement.\n\n - Bring audience and market insight into product development, from early strategy through launch and iteration.\n\n - Define success measures, design experiments, and use adoption, engagement, conversion, and revenue data to evaluate impact and adjust the strategy.\n\nWhat You Bring\n\n - 5+ years of experience in product marketing or a closely related role, ideally in a consumer technology environment.\n\n - Exceptional writing skills and the ability to make complex products clear, compelling, and trustworthy.\n\n - A track record of developing positioning and messaging and leading go-to-market strategy for new or evolving products.\n\n - Hands-on experience writing lifecycle communications that support onboarding, engagement, retention, or reactivation.\n\n - Strong audience orientation and a practical approach to using qualitative and quantitative insights to make decisions.\n\n - A track record of setting measurable goals, designing experiments, and using adoption, engagement, conversion, and revenue data to evaluate impact.\n\n - Comfort operating autonomously in a fast-moving environment, creating structure from ambiguity, adapting as priorities shift, and building buy-in across teams.\n\nEspecially Helpful\n\n - Experience marketing products in benefits, healthcare, Medicare, financial technology, or another complex or highly regulated consumer category.\n\nAt Propel, you'll enjoy:\n\n - Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission\n\n - Remote-friendly work environment with a dog-friendly office in Downtown Brooklyn. The team meets in-person for optional retreats a few times per year.\n\n - 20 Days of PTO\n\n - 4% 401K match\n\n - $10k lifetime spend towards Carrot Fertility\n\n - Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision options\n\n - Other health and mental health focused benefits and perks\n\n - Propel builds compensation bands referencing the 75th percentile of compensation for companies like us. Expected compensation for the role as scoped is $125,000 - $175,000 and will be based on how a candidate matches to our internal leveling guide.\n\nAdditional Considerations:\n\n - We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.\n\n - We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Virginia, and Washington.\n\n - Background Check Requirement: For roles with access to confidential employee or customer information, a background check may be conducted following a conditional offer. All background checks are handled in accordance with applicable laws, including the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA).\n\nMore About Propel\n\nPropel is a technology company that’s strengthening the social safety net for people who receive government benefits. Over 5 million Americans trust the free, modern Propel app to manage their government benefits, save money, and get updates when their benefits change. We’ve also partnered with renowned institutions and organizations like Vote.org http://Vote.org, GoFundMe, and GiveDirectly.\n\nPropel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We're proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors, including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.\n\nLearn more about our impact from the press\n\n - Fintech Company Propel Announces $10 Million Fund For Food Stamp https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - Late Show With Stephen Colbert http://linkedin.com/posts/givedirectly_help-feed-snap-families-missing-their-benefits-activity-7391501043743870977-UeOM?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAAA1BqiYB0lii8Gct_U9ZZcrAcq9V9vnIZuU\n\n - How to Propel the Fight Against Poverty in America https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VJpjAwxAciA\n\n - How Tech is Helping Poor People Get Government Aid https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/08/us/politics/safety-net-apps-tech.html?partner=slack&smid=sl-share\n\n - Propel Routes Money to those Who Need it Most https://www.forbes.com/sites/jeffkauflin/2020/04/03/fintech-apps-offer-first-aid-for-hardest-hit-consumers/#70df70611a93\n\n - How one tech startup is giving cash to SNAP recipients https://www.npr.org/2025/11/04/nx-s1-5587728/snap-shutdown-propel-tech-startup-cash-donations\n\n - Recipients Affected By Government Shutdown https://www.forbes.com/sites/juliegoldenberg/2025/10/30/fintech-company-propel-announces-10-million-fund-for-food-stamp-recipients-affected-by-government-shutdown/\n\n - How hunger relief groups say you can help feed your neighbors during the shutdown and beyond https://apnews.com/article/food-banks-snap-benefits-freeze-3c232305bfe0fbaea9efc795c8c07a99\n\n - Helping our Users Navigate this Crisis https://www.joinpropel.com/covid-19\n\nJoin us, and let's build something amazing together!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"71314cfd-8757-4051-ae80-d8711413ad48","title":"Senior Customer Success Manager ","department":"Customer Success","team":"Customer Success","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"USA","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-24T21:05:08.560+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/71314cfd-8757-4051-ae80-d8711413ad48","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/propel/71314cfd-8757-4051-ae80-d8711413ad48/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Us</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel builds technology that strengthens the social safety net in America. We envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The safety net’s strength depends not just on funding, but delivery. Propel exists to dramatically improve how government benefits are delivered. Managing SNAP benefits, picking a D-SNP plan, or protecting against EBT theft should feel as seamless as Apple Pay or Netflix.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Governments struggle to build modern, scalable user experiences. We don’t.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Over 5 million Americans trust Propel today. We’ve grown revenue 35% YoY and are reinventing entire benefit categories, including Medicare, around the real needs of low-income Americans. We’re building a high-growth, high-ceiling, sustainable for-profit company where impact drives revenue.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>The Role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a results-oriented <strong>Senior Customer Success Manager</strong> to join our advertising business unit, helping companies in a variety of sectors effectively market to low-income consumers via the <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.propel.app/\"><u>Propel</u></a> app. You’ll report directly to the Director of Customer Success.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll manage a portfolio of accounts, developing strong customer relationships and driving growth toward a revenue target. Our partners advertise mission-aligned products and services that help our users make it through the month. These partnerships are a core part of how we scale our impact: helping our users sign up for discounted home internet and government-subsidized phone plans, promoting grocery discounts and savings, and enrolling people in energy assistance programs, just to name a few.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You’ll be responsible for:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Owning a portfolio of accounts generating $8-$20 million in annual revenue, </strong>with strong growth potential</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Implementing and optimizing marketing campaigns for your accounts, </strong>delivering great results that meet your customers’ goals</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Growing your portfolio </strong>by identifying opportunities to sell new placements and campaigns and increase budgets or pricing in ways that optimize existing campaigns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Helping us build more scalable and efficient Customer Success tools </strong>by partnering with your product and tech counterparts to improve our systems</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Serve as a strategic partner and subject matter expert</strong> for customers, proactively offering recommendations and guidance to help them achieve their goals in reaching lower-income consumers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Owning the commercial strategy for your vertical, </strong>building out a GTM strategy, ensuring we have the materials and story needed to sell, and partnering internally to optimize placements and campaigns for your vertical</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Proactively sharing learnings with teammates </strong>to improve our collective understanding of industry trends and best practices</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Requirements:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">8+ years of enterprise customer success or account management experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with digital marketing at either a publisher, agency, or advertiser</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exceptional written and oral presentation and communication skills. You’ll spend a lot of time in front of your customers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong problem-solving and project management abilities. You’ll be responsible for campaign troubleshooting, launch timelines, experimentation management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated ability to juggle competing priorities and navigate ambiguity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong attention to detail and comfort navigating technical systems - you’ll be responsible for implementing new campaigns, analyzing performance data, and identifying optimization opportunities</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent relationship-building skills, with a demonstrated ability to quickly build trust internally and externally</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Passion for building a business with a strong social mission at the intersection of private and public sectors</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to travel to conduct strategic planning sessions with key accounts at least once per quarter</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>At Propel, you'll enjoy:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Remote-friendly work environment with a dog-friendly office in Downtown Brooklyn</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">All-company retreats and team on-sites roughly twice per year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">20 Days of PTO</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4% 401K match</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$10k lifetime fertility expense reimbursement via Carrot Fertility</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision insurance options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Free access to Ginger mental health, Gympass, Headspace, One Medical, Rightway, Sofi, and Spring Health</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel believes that everyone should be compensated fairly and equitably. We set our salary ranges using compensation data from hundreds of NYC-based startups at our stage. Additionally, pay is not determined based on location. Compensation for this position includes base salary and a performance-based bonus. <strong>The expected base salary for the role is $150,000 - $180,000</strong>. The bonus is a combination of individual and team revenue performance. <strong>The total on-target earnings (OTE) is $165,000 - $198,000</strong>. There is potential for a larger bonus if individual and/or team revenue targets are exceeded. Equity and excellent benefits come with this position as well!</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Additional Considerations:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes <strong>California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Utah, Virginia, and Washington.</strong></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>More About Propel</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We believe that Americans with limited income deserve modern, respectful, and effective experiences around their government benefits and money. Unfortunately, the status quo often fails to treat them as first-class citizens in their daily interactions around the social safety net and financial services. The tech industry hasn’t pulled its weight in solving the problems faced by low-income Americans.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel’s mission is to change that. We’ve built Propel, the single most popular app in the country built specifically for low-income Americans. Over 5 million families each month use Propel to seamlessly manage their government benefits (programs like SNAP, commonly known as food stamps)and save and earn money. Propel has been recognized by the White House, featured on the front page of the NYTimes, and carries over 500,000 five star reviews.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Propel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We’re proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors, including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Join us, and let's build something amazing together!</strong></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT US\n\nPropel builds technology that strengthens the social safety net in America. We envision a future where every American has the tools and resources they need to thrive.\n\nThe safety net’s strength depends not just on funding, but delivery. Propel exists to dramatically improve how government benefits are delivered. Managing SNAP benefits, picking a D-SNP plan, or protecting against EBT theft should feel as seamless as Apple Pay or Netflix.\n\nGovernments struggle to build modern, scalable user experiences. We don’t.\n\nOver 5 million Americans trust Propel today. We’ve grown revenue 35% YoY and are reinventing entire benefit categories, including Medicare, around the real needs of low-income Americans. We’re building a high-growth, high-ceiling, sustainable for-profit company where impact drives revenue.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nWe’re looking for a results-oriented Senior Customer Success Manager to join our advertising business unit, helping companies in a variety of sectors effectively market to low-income consumers via the Propel https://www.propel.app/ app. You’ll report directly to the Director of Customer Success.\n\nYou’ll manage a portfolio of accounts, developing strong customer relationships and driving growth toward a revenue target. Our partners advertise mission-aligned products and services that help our users make it through the month. These partnerships are a core part of how we scale our impact: helping our users sign up for discounted home internet and government-subsidized phone plans, promoting grocery discounts and savings, and enrolling people in energy assistance programs, just to name a few.\n\nYou’ll be responsible for:\n\n - Owning a portfolio of accounts generating $8-$20 million in annual revenue, with strong growth potential\n\n - Implementing and optimizing marketing campaigns for your accounts, delivering great results that meet your customers’ goals\n\n - Growing your portfolio by identifying opportunities to sell new placements and campaigns and increase budgets or pricing in ways that optimize existing campaigns\n\n - Helping us build more scalable and efficient Customer Success tools by partnering with your product and tech counterparts to improve our systems\n\n - Serve as a strategic partner and subject matter expert for customers, proactively offering recommendations and guidance to help them achieve their goals in reaching lower-income consumers\n\n - Owning the commercial strategy for your vertical, building out a GTM strategy, ensuring we have the materials and story needed to sell, and partnering internally to optimize placements and campaigns for your vertical\n\n - Proactively sharing learnings with teammates to improve our collective understanding of industry trends and best practices\n\nRequirements:\n\n - 8+ years of enterprise customer success or account management experience\n\n - Experience with digital marketing at either a publisher, agency, or advertiser\n\n - Exceptional written and oral presentation and communication skills. You’ll spend a lot of time in front of your customers\n\n - Strong problem-solving and project management abilities. You’ll be responsible for campaign troubleshooting, launch timelines, experimentation management\n\n - Demonstrated ability to juggle competing priorities and navigate ambiguity\n\n - Strong attention to detail and comfort navigating technical systems - you’ll be responsible for implementing new campaigns, analyzing performance data, and identifying optimization opportunities\n\n - Excellent relationship-building skills, with a demonstrated ability to quickly build trust internally and externally\n\n - Passion for building a business with a strong social mission at the intersection of private and public sectors\n\n - Willingness to travel to conduct strategic planning sessions with key accounts at least once per quarter\n\nAt Propel, you'll enjoy:\n\n - Meaningful work and a strong shared sense of mission\n\n - Remote-friendly work environment with a dog-friendly office in Downtown Brooklyn\n\n - All-company retreats and team on-sites roughly twice per year\n\n - 20 Days of PTO\n\n - 4% 401K match\n\n - $10k lifetime fertility expense reimbursement via Carrot Fertility\n\n - Excellent Medical, Dental and Vision insurance options\n\n - Free access to Ginger mental health, Gympass, Headspace, One Medical, Rightway, Sofi, and Spring Health\n\n - Propel believes that everyone should be compensated fairly and equitably. We set our salary ranges using compensation data from hundreds of NYC-based startups at our stage. Additionally, pay is not determined based on location. Compensation for this position includes base salary and a performance-based bonus. The expected base salary for the role is $150,000 - $180,000. The bonus is a combination of individual and team revenue performance. The total on-target earnings (OTE) is $165,000 - $198,000. There is potential for a larger bonus if individual and/or team revenue targets are exceeded. Equity and excellent benefits come with this position as well!\n\nAdditional Considerations:\n\n - We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive team, and welcome applicants from all backgrounds and abilities.\n\n - We're currently accepting applications from the states we have an established entity, which includes California, Colorado, District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, Illinois, Maryland, Massachusetts, New Jersey, New York, Oregon, Pennsylvania, Texas, Utah, Virginia, and Washington.\n\nMore About Propel\n\nWe believe that Americans with limited income deserve modern, respectful, and effective experiences around their government benefits and money. Unfortunately, the status quo often fails to treat them as first-class citizens in their daily interactions around the social safety net and financial services. The tech industry hasn’t pulled its weight in solving the problems faced by low-income Americans.\n\nPropel’s mission is to change that. We’ve built Propel, the single most popular app in the country built specifically for low-income Americans. Over 5 million families each month use Propel to seamlessly manage their government benefits (programs like SNAP, commonly known as food stamps)and save and earn money. Propel has been recognized by the White House, featured on the front page of the NYTimes, and carries over 500,000 five star reviews.\n\nPropel is a for-profit, venture-backed company that holds its social mission at its core. We’re proud to be supported by a blend of nonprofits, impact investors, and world-class investors, including the Robin Hood Foundation, Andreessen Horowitz, Nyca Partners, Financial Health Network, JPMorganChase, Kevin Durant, Serena Williams, and Nas.\n\nJoin us, and let's build something amazing together!","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}